## Spatial Composition
Top-anchored heading, then italic thesis subhead below. Three equal columns below: left column covers technology opportunities with bold subheader, middle column addresses structural challenges with bold subheader, right column presents strategic implications with bold subheader. Each column contains 2-3 sentences of dense prose. Summary grid layout for comprehensive landscape recap.

## Card Content (HTML)
<h1>Climate Tech's Commercial Moment Arrives Amid Structural Headwinds</h1>
    <p>Climate technology reaches commercial inflection points across energy storage, green hydrogen, and carbon capture as costs achieve fossil fuel parity and investment capital flows reach record levels. Technology maturation combines with manufacturing scale effects to create self-reinforcing adoption cycles that position clean energy for market dominance within this decade.</p>
    <p>However, structural barriers constrain deployment velocity despite favorable economics. Regulatory uncertainty adds 200-400 basis points to project financing costs. Critical mineral supply chains create bottlenecks that will limit battery production through 2027. Talent shortages across specialized engineering roles extend project development timelines and increase operational costs.</p>
    <p>Strategic success requires navigating this paradox: breakthrough technology economics amid persistent deployment friction. Organizations that solve regulatory navigation, secure supply chain partnerships, and build specialized talent capabilities will capture disproportionate value as climate tech transitions from venture-backed experimentation to industrial-scale commercial deployment.</p>

## Context
Deck intent: Authoritative climate tech landscape analysis with data-heavy prose and stark visual contrasts. Use dark backgrounds with bright accent colors to convey urgency. Charts and statistics integrated into dense text blocks. Professional tone with environmental stakes made visceral through specific examples and projections.
Card instructions: Summary/closing card: 'Climate Tech's Commercial Moment Arrives Amid Structural Headwinds'. Multi-column recap of key opportunities (technology maturation, cost competitiveness, investment flows) and persistent challenges (regulatory, supply chain, talent). 100 words synthesizing the landscape for strategic decision-making.

## Art Direction (MUST follow)
This climate tech landscape analysis demands a stark, data-driven aesthetic that matches the urgency and gravity of the subject matter. Use dark backgrounds—deep charcoal or black—as the primary canvas to create a sense of environmental crisis and technical sophistication. Against these dark foundations, deploy bright accent colors strategically: electric blues for breakthrough technologies, sharp greens for commercial successes, and warning oranges or reds for barriers and constraints. This high-contrast approach should feel authoritative and urgent, like reading a critical intelligence briefing under emergency lighting.

Every card must integrate dense statistical information seamlessly into flowing prose using the stats smart layout variant. When presenting breakthrough cost declines, investment figures, or production scales, embed these numbers as hero statistics within explanatory paragraphs—never let data stand naked without interpretation. Use the outlineBoxes smart layout sparingly and only for structural comparisons like the four key sectors or three systemic barriers. The typography should emphasize hierarchy through bold H1 titles that read like authoritative declarations, with H4 subheaders in columns breaking up dense technical prose. Employ strategic color spans on critical metrics and breakthrough moments—highlight "$165 billion," "89% cost decline," and "sub-$100 per ton" in accent colors to make the data visceral and immediate. Blockquotes should capture industry voices that validate the analysis, set against accent backgrounds to break the rhythm of technical density. Avoid any presentation-style flourishes—no solid boxes, no decorative elements. This document should read like an authoritative technical report where every visual choice reinforces the message that climate technology has reached a pivotal, urgent moment demanding immediate attention and investment.

## Allowed Variants (structural reference)
- boxes: outlineBoxes
- stats: stats
Max families per deck: 1
Use ONLY variants from the allowed list. The art direction above tells you WHICH to pick and WHEN.

## Image Layout
image-layout="blank". No image on this card.

Translate to a single <SECTION> block of valid GML.
